# Advanced-manufacturing lens: scoping runs (15 kW, 18 LPM PG25, 45 C, 117 cm2 unless stated)

## 0. Validation against the project model
model HMMC-R PCM: avg 28.05 max 31.05 dP 5.32 kPa; this script: avg 28.05 max 31.05 dP 5.72 kPa (= model + 0.4 kPa clean screen)

## 1. Fin-conduction ceiling at a fixed channel gap (straight plate fins, any process, infinite height)
| gap mm | h (4 mm cell) kW/m2K | ceiling h_eff Cu 390 | opt. fin t mm | ceiling ECAM 370 | ceiling L-PBF 340 | ceiling Cu-diamond fins 600 (not makeable) | achieved by skived core |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| 0.10 | 19.8 | 207 | 0.09 | 202 | 194 | 254 | 187 (P core 0.10/0.10x1.5) |
| 0.15 | 13.2 | 138 | 0.14 | 134 | 129 | 169 | 127 (R core 0.15/0.10x2.0); 135 at H 3 mm |
| 0.20 | 9.9 | 104 | 0.18 | 101 | 97 | 127 | 87-98 |
| 0.40 | 5.3 | 53 | 0.36 | 52 | 50 | 66 | - |

Reading: at the 0.15 mm fouling floor no copper plate-fin geometry exceeds ~138 kW/m2K; the skived R core is at 92 % of it (98 % at 3 mm fins). Resolution buys nothing once the gap is fixed by filtration.

